                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df1e6ad9-3260-3e86-9571-b5b755edffb0",
                        "entry_id": "71f05fa0-0bc4-3982-9bc9-ba6bd88073e9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "powstający spontanicznie lub mający niejasne albo nieznane podłoże"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "42ff1933-88bc-45de-9d02-29fe7838ff22",
                        "source_entry_id": "71f05fa0-0bc4-3982-9bc9-ba6bd88073e9",
                        "source_sense_id": "df1e6ad9-3260-3e86-9571-b5b755edffb0",
                        "target_lang_word": "idiopathic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "idiopathic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "311faa3f-9b24-374d-b9cc-5747cd14ccf6",
                                        "entry_id": "2a562c1d-8fda-32b6-bfba-cc69dafed0e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, or designating a disease or condition having no known cause."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27e2370d-610c-4346-a1ca-921f90dd7330",
                                                "sense_id": "311faa3f-9b24-374d-b9cc-5747cd14ccf6",
                                                "text": "So when I was diagnosed with a fairly difficult-to-treat disease called idiopathic angioedema and chronic urticaria (a fancy way of saying we don’t know why you swell and hey, enjoy the 24/7 hives) six months ago, I wasn't quite sure how to cope."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9622792-12f5-45a7-ba69-d24a9d32d515",
                                                "sense_id": "311faa3f-9b24-374d-b9cc-5747cd14ccf6",
                                                "text": "Juvenile rheumatoid arthritis (JRA), often referred to by doctors today as juvenile idiopathic arthritis (JIA), is a type of arthritis that causes joint inflammation and stiffness for more than six weeks in a child aged 16 or younger. It affects approximately 50,000 children in the United States. Inflammation causes redness, swelling, warmth, and soreness in the joints, although many children with JRA do not complain of joint pain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "20f8b992-d31f-45d6-b2e5-e9e69783dfe4",
                        "source_entry_id": "71f05fa0-0bc4-3982-9bc9-ba6bd88073e9",
                        "source_sense_id": "df1e6ad9-3260-3e86-9571-b5b755edffb0",
                        "target_lang_word": "idiopathique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "idiopathique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6831bfb1-9958-3d5f-aebc-c9304aa3ee96",
                                        "entry_id": "c51c791d-0740-361d-b67b-eed024e05de7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a le caractère de l’idiopathie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90672162-6cc3-42ba-b6b8-2ee93979bc21",
                                                "sense_id": "6831bfb1-9958-3d5f-aebc-c9304aa3ee96",
                                                "text": "Quant à la surdité qui est due à des convulsions depuis longtemps guéries, elle rentre dans la classe des acousies idiopathiques, et les moyens thérapeutiques que nous avons conseillés contre cette dernière névrose lui sont applicables."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d35ead72-97e3-4af7-8b82-2610381fe0c8",
                                                "sense_id": "6831bfb1-9958-3d5f-aebc-c9304aa3ee96",
                                                "text": "Les névroses idiopathiques de la vie de relation, dont le siége peut être dans les expansions ou les cordons nerveux, sont également précédées de phlegmasies, lorsque l’inflammation, en ramollissant les tissus, a exalté la sensibilité, au point de développer des névralgies, des mouvemens convulsifs, des paralysies, a augmenté, diminué ou aboli l’irritabilité des expansions vasculo-nerveuses qui forment les sens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
